[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +This is the sole successor dispatcher for the unresolved QB-A editorial
[stderr] +records recorded by `GD0002`. It preserves the existing 48-card boundary and
[stderr] +does not create cards, publish cards, alter quiz scope, create B/R runbooks, or
[stderr] +accept `../planning/game-design-manifest.json`.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The current register deliberately records all 48 revision-1 cards as `draft`
[stderr] +and `selectionEligible: false`. Every card retains the exact reasons
[stderr] +`ORIGINALITY-UNAUTHORED`, `PROVENANCE-LOCATOR-MISSING`,
[stderr] +`FACTUAL-RIGHTS-REVIEW-PENDING`, `ACCESSIBILITY-COPY-REVIEW-PENDING`, and
[stderr] +`RELEASE-GATE-INCOMPLETE`. No default, batch-level decision, or future wave
[stderr] +may substitute for a card's current-revision evidence.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Bounded editorial waves
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Each wave below is limited to one existing 12-card batch. Within a wave, author
[stderr] +evidence first and review it only after the current-revision authoring evidence
[stderr] +is complete. A card that is rejected, unresolved, conflicted, withdrawn, or
[stderr] +missing any required record stays ineligible with its exact reason retained.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Wave | Existing batch | Fixed card IDs | Required card-level work | Completion boundary |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| E1 | `GPI-002` — World Tournament History | `QB-A-01`–`QB-A-12` | Original expression; exact permitted-source locators and checked dates for every assertion; conflict/correction state; factual/rights review; accessibility/copy review; independent second review. | 12 current-revision records only. |
[stderr] +| E2 | `GPI-003` — Domestic League Moments | `QB-A-13`–`QB-A-24` | Same evidence and distinct-review requirements as E1. | 12 current-revision records only. |
[stderr] +| E3 | `GPI-004` — Club, Manager, and Identity | `QB-A-25`–`QB-A-36` | Same evidence and distinct-review requirements as E1, including both permitted source routes where stated. | 12 current-revision records only. |
[stderr] +| E4 | `GPI-005` — Players and Records | `QB-A-37`–`QB-A-48` | Same evidence and distinct-review requirements as E1. | 12 current-revision records only. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +For every card, the factual/rights and accessibility/copy decisions must be
[stderr] +accepted by distinct reviewers for the exact revision. The release editor may
[stderr] +set `published` only after those accepted decisions, accepted originality and
[stderr] +provenance evidence, no unresolved conflict, and the defined lifecycle
[stderr] +transitions. Until then a selector must reject it because the register's
[stderr] +selection rule remains binding.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## GQ audit gate
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not create a `GQ` audit while any of the 48 records remains un-authored,
[stderr] +pending, blocked, rejected, conflicted, withdrawn, or otherwise ineligible.
[stderr] +Only after all four waves contain actual accepted evidence may a later `GQ`
[stderr] +audit run the dedicated completion check, update canonical bible/inventory
[stderr] +records, and accept the manifest. This dispatcher does none of those actions.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- The QB-A catalogue remains exactly four existing named batches of 12 cards
[stderr] +  (48 IDs total), with no replacement or added card.
[stderr] +- Each still-ineligible card retains its exact reason and cannot enter
[stderr] +  selection until current-revision evidence and two distinct accepted reviews
[stderr] +  qualify it.
[stderr] +- No `GQ` audit is created and the manifest remains pending until all 48
[stderr] +  records have actual accepted evidence.
